:: Booze Night [event mom_quest] {"position":"4025,1075","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Booze Night" (mom_boozeNight), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 5.1. The breather after A Knock at Night: a weeknight, a bottle
   of wine in the living room, no device. She talks about $dad.callName and how long it has been since anyone chose her. I don't
   do anything. I listen and let her wait, her lust climbs, and she goes to bed having asked for nothing.
   It unlocks catching her at home (micro events 46 to 48, Mom Catch Couch/Kitchen/Shower). */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[2].img>><</silent>>
The living room is dark except for the lamp by the couch and the TV, which is on with the sound off. Some cooking show. A man is folding egg whites into something with the solemn face of a surgeon.

$mom.callName is in her corner of the couch with her feet tucked under her and a glass of red in her hand. The bottle is on the coffee table, a little less than half full. It's a Tuesday, or a Wednesday, one of the days that don't count, and she has a coaster under the bottle and another one under her glass, which is how I know she had a plan when she opened it.

<<Media "images/characters/mom/events/booze_night/couch.jpg" 600>>
/* Mom curled up in the corner of the couch in leggings and an oversized cardigan, a glass of red wine, the TV light on her face */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh. Hi, honey. I didn't hear you come down." },
{ text: "She looks at the bottle as if somebody else had left it there." },
{ who: $mom, text: "It was open. Well, it wasn't, but it was sitting in the cupboard behind the olive oil and it would have gone bad eventually, so really I'm saving it. Do you want a glass? You probably have work, you don't have to keep me company." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Get a glass">>
I get a glass from the kitchen and sit down at the other end of the couch, not in the middle. She pours for me with great care, filling it exactly as far as hers, and then tops hers up a little so they match again.

For a while we watch the man with the egg whites. His soufflé collapses. She makes a small sympathetic noise, the one she used to make when I struck out at Little League.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Your $dad.relation used to cook on Sundays, did you know that? Before you two came along. He made this awful chili with so much cumin in it, sweetie, you could smell it on the curtains for a week." },
{ who: $player, text: "Wait, he cooked? I don't think I ever saw him do more than stand next to the grill." },
{ who: $mom, text: "He stopped when your $sister.relation came, and then you, and there just wasn't time for chili anymore, or for a lot of things, and then he was traveling so much, and then..." },
{ text: "She waves her glass at the rest of the sentence. A little wine slops up the side and she watches it slide back down." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Anyway, that's ancient history, honey. I might as well be telling you about the Romans." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Let her keep going">>
I don't say anything. With her, if I leave a quiet long enough, she fills it, and after a minute she does.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "You know what I was thinking about today, at my desk? It's so silly." },
{ who: $mom, text: "When I met your $dad.relation I was at a party with my roommate, and I was in the kitchen, because I'm always in the kitchen at parties, somebody has to make sure there's ice. And he walked all the way across that room, past all these girls who were so much prettier than me and so much more interesting, right into the kitchen. To me. He picked me out of a whole room." },
{ text: "She smiles into her glass, and then the smile goes somewhere else." },
{ who: $mom, text: "And I don't think anybody has picked me since. Isn't that a funny thing to figure out at my age? People pick me to organize the bake sale, or to take the minutes, or to call the caterer, and that's nice, I like being useful, but that's not... that isn't what I mean." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She laughs at herself, because that's what she does when she's said too much, and drinks to cover the laugh. Her cheeks are pink, and the cardigan has slipped off one shoulder without her fixing it, which is unusual for a woman who fixes everything, other people's collars included.

<<linkreplace "Say nothing">>
I could tell her that I picked her. That I pick her all the time now: for the sixth floor, for the meeting room, for the test sessions in the evening. That I picked her out of a whole house. She'd hear it as something sweet, and it would be the kindest thing anyone has said to her in a year.

I drink my wine instead and keep looking at her, and let her wonder what I'm thinking.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "What? Why are you looking at me like that, do I have wine on my chin?" },
{ who: $player, text: "No, you're fine. I'm just listening." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Well, you're looking at me like you're waiting for something, honey." },
{ who: $player, text: "Maybe I'm waiting for the rest of the story. You stopped right in the middle." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Nobody listens to me this long, you know that? Your $sister.relation gets about two sentences in before her phone buzzes. You'll give me a big head." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She tucks her feet in tighter. A minute later she untucks them again, and her toes end up a few inches from my thigh, and she leaves them there and pretends that they're not there, and I pretend with her.

<<linkreplace "Let the bottle run out">>
The bottle goes down. She does most of the work. She tells me about the roommate, who married a dentist, and about the first apartment, which had a bathtub in the kitchen, and about her favorite dress, a navy one at the back of her closet that she's hardly ever worn, because there's never anywhere nice enough to wear it to, and anyway, she says into her glass, who would she wear it for.

Every time she stops talking she looks at me, and every time I just wait, and every time she starts talking again a little faster. She keeps touching her own collarbone. She keeps crossing and uncrossing her legs. At one point she gets up to get water, and stands at the kitchen counter for a long time with the glass in her hand and her back to me, and doesn't drink any of it.

I'm fairly sure I know what she wants. The night she came up to my room, she told me to come and find her whenever it gets bad. Tonight it's bad for her, not for me, and she never made a rule for that. If I reached over now, I think she'd let me, and tomorrow she'd tell herself it was the wine.

I'd rather she didn't have the wine to blame, so I keep both hands on my glass.

<<linkreplace "Say goodnight">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "It's getting late, and you've got that client call at nine." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, God, nine, you're right, and I haven't even looked at their file again." },
{ text: "She stands up too fast, steadies herself on the armrest and laughs about it. She picks up both glasses and the empty bottle and stands there holding them, looking at me." },
{ who: $mom, text: "This was nice, honey, just sitting here talking like this. We should do it more often, we should... well. It was nice." },
{ who: $player, text: "It was. Drink a glass of water before you go to sleep, okay?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "Listen to you. Goodnight, sweetheart." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She takes the glasses to the kitchen. I hear her rinse them, slowly, and set them upside down on the rack. Then the stairs, one at a time, and on the landing a pause where she stands still for a few seconds before she goes on.

Her door closes. A while later, through the ceiling, I hear her bed creak once, and then again, and then for a long time in a rhythm she probably thinks is quiet.

I turn the TV off and finish my glass in the dark. Somewhere around the last sip it occurs to me that $company.prototype.name has been sitting in my desk drawer all evening, switched off, and I never once thought about it.

